<item>
            <title>[PARQUET-2342] Parquet writer produced a corrupted file due to page value count overflow</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/PARQUET-2342</link>
                <project id="12315521" key="PARQUET">Parquet</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Parquet writer only checks the number of rows and the page size to decide whether it needs to fit a content to be written in a single page.&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In the case of a composite column (ex: array/map) with a lot of nulls, it is possible to create 2billions+ values while under the default page-size &amp;amp; row-count threshold (1MB, 20000rows)&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Repro using Spark:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;tt&gt;&#160; &#160; &#160; val dir = &quot;/tmp/anyrandomDirectory&quot;&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;tt&gt;&#160; &#160; &#160; spark.range(0, 20000, 1, 1)&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;tt&gt;&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; .selectExpr(&quot;array_repeat(cast(null as binary), 110000) as n&quot;)&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;tt&gt;&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; .write&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;tt&gt;&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; .mode(&quot;overwrite&quot;)&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;tt&gt;&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; .save(dir)&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;tt&gt;&#160; &#160; &#160; val result = spark&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;tt&gt;&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; .sql(s&quot;select * from parquet.`$dir` limit 1000&quot;)&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;tt&gt;&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; .collect() // This will break&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
